<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eighth Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1270</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eighth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was the expedition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> in 1270. The crusaders landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in July, hoping to convert or subdue the Hafsid ruler al-Mustansir, but disease swept the camp and Louis died there in August. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a> negotiated a treaty by which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsids</a> paid an indemnity and renewed tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, and the army withdrew.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eighth-crusade.jpg" alt="Eighth Crusade" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Fouquet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SmrtLudvika91270.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
